WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:05.434
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.844 --> 00:00:16.239
INES TORRES: Before Djoser adopted the pyramid two model,

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:19.870
the kings of the first dynasty were buried in highly complex mud brick

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:25.100
structures, sunk in the desert and divided into several chambers.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.540
Some of these earlier royal tombs had an extraordinary monumental character

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.490
which reveals the already complex level of the society that builds such tombs.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.880
Djoser was not only the first king who used stone as a material

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.960
for royal tomb building, but also the first king to build a pyramid.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.280
It is also important to stress that his pyramid represents

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.460
an unequaled innovation in monumental construction,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.880
both in size and materials used.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.240
Djoser's pyramid was built in stages, beginning as the square mastaba

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.890
and eventually being transformed into the final six step pyramid.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.610
It is unclear what the process of building Djoser's pyramid

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.050
actually entailed.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.260
But Jean-Philippe Lauer who excavated the site

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.190
believes that the pyramid was built in six different stages.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.800
If one assumes that this is correct, then there

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:21.800
was a major enlargement every three years, for Djoser reigned for 19 years.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.090
The implications of building such a complex,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.610
which was the size of a large town, in the third millennium BCE, cannot be

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.560
emphasized enough.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.710
Indeed, this would require tight political control

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.850
of the people and resources of Egypt at an early period.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:42.800
Djoser's pyramid complex is unique in that it is oriented north-south rather

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.490
than east-west like the Giza pyramids, and possesses

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:50.730
a number of buildings and structures which are not seen elsewhere.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.730
It is thought that Djoser's pyramid complex

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:57.110
was intended to model Egypt mainly because of its north-south division

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.700
and because of the symbolism of the buildings within this complex.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.150
It was the first king of the Fourth Dynasty, Sneferu,

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.880
who built the first true pyramid.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.759
His reign is particularly interesting for Sneferu

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:16.010
built several pyramids before being able to attain the true pyramidal form.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:20.540
One can see obvious continuation from several of Sneferu's pyramid complexes

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.120
to those at Giza.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.790
Just like the step pyramid built by Djoser,

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.640
Sneferu's first attempt at a pyramid at Meidum

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.170
was built in stages, starting with a seven step pyramid.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.730
This was afterwards enlarged to a pyramid of eight steps.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.330
Later in his reign, Sneferu sent his workmen back to Meidum

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:46.490
to fill out the original step pyramid as a true pyramid.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:50.450
One of the new features of the pyramid complex introduced in Meidum

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:55.550
was the causeway which was to become standard for such monuments.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:58.160
For reasons unknown, Sneferu abandoned Meidum

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.160
and founded a new cemetery in Dashur.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.930
There he built two other large pyramids known as the Bent and Red or North

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.340
pyramids.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.950
The Bent pyramid started as a smaller pyramid

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.980
with a slope of about 60 degrees.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.950
Faced with some structural problems with the foundation,

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.690
the builders of this pyramid had to adjust the slope to around 55 degrees.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.000
Since the stress on the pyramid was too great

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.350
and the structure lacked stability, as reflected in its pronounced bend,

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:32.690
this monument was abandoned and a new pyramid was started in North Dashur.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.360
Around year 30 of his reign, Sneferu started

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.870
work of the Red pyramid, which was built at a much gentler slope than the Bent

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:43.880
pyramid and was also made very carefully from the beginning.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.780
This project resulted in the true pyramidal form.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:51.350
The paradigm of the true pyramidal form occurs at Giza.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.130
The pyramids here were built over the span of three generations.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.950
Khufu was the founder of the Giza cemetery

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:03.080
and the builder of the first and tallest pyramid ever built in Egypt.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.780
At Giza, the Old Kingdom pyramid complex,

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.570
namely the mortuary and valley temples, was expanded and standardized.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.610
The period causeways were extended to nearly 1 kilometer

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.290
and reached the Nile and the Valley Temple.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:22.070
Khufu's wall and causeway even defined an area of harbors, settlement,

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.550
and possibly a palace by the river.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.670
The mastaba tombs that surrounded Khufu's pyramid also

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:31.760
represented a new form of necropolis arrangement,

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.030
with its orthogonal design giving the idea of an organized

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:39.320
city of the dead with streets and a preconceived plan.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.720
The three different pyramid complexes at Giza

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.480
were enclosed by stone and clay walls which

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:50.390
are still partially preserved around the complexes of Khafre and Menkaure.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.790
It is not clear how these three pyramids were actually built.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.030
But it is important to notice that this was

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:59.810
the result of many years of experimenting and pyramid building.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.000
Note that Khufu was Sneferu's son.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.600
And as such, the workers and architects of the Great Pyramid

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.750
had already acquired sufficient knowledge and skills

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.860
to take this leap forward.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:14.480
After Sneferu, it appears that the technique for pyramid building

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.800
was standardized.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.660
And step pyramids were never built again in Egypt.

